Hanumān leads Tāra Aṅgada into Vindhya caves thickets --- Monkeys eat roots fruits finding neither Sītā nor Rāvaṇa --- Monkeys enter barren waterless root-scarce fearless forest --- Monkeys learn Kaṇḍu curse emptied woods of beasts birds --- Monkeys search forest ends caves river sources vainly --- Monkeys confront cruel god-fearless mountainlike asura --- Aṅgada fells rusher mistaking him for Rāvaṇa --- Victors search caves again then sit dejected hopeless
